10. Consolidated Action Items

The following list combines the explicit action items from the supplied meeting summaries with the operational follow-ups described in the sessions.

Regression screenshots: Capture screenshots during the regression run and combine the team screenshots into one consolidated document.

Broken HTTP monitor: Investigate the currently failing monitor, identify the returned error/underlying problem, and restore it to working condition.

Shared tracker: Upload the existing server monitoring spreadsheet to the shared Dynatrace/SharePoint folder.

Firewall status: Update the tracker with firewall status for non-production and production OnBase servers.

AMD software folder: Verify the AMD software download folder/location exists and is accessible; provide the confirmed location to the security team.

PAD coordination: Coordinate with PAD for the required installation activity and validate the resulting Dynatrace service/agent status.

Non-production AMDR access: Request the relevant group/Zach for access needed to test RUM configuration in non-production/regression.

OnBase production onboarding: Complete the remaining steps to add the new OnBase production servers to Dynatrace and validate reporting.

Regression cleanup: Restore important regression applications/monitors to a healthy state so failures can be found early.

Portal dashboard access: Share the internal portal performance dashboard and ensure team members can access it.

Change tracking discipline: Record every relevant Dynatrace configuration change in the tracker, including production/non-production changes, RUM, monitoring mode and enable/disable actions.

11. Daily / Periodic Operational Checklist

Use this as a lightweight operational routine derived from the KT discussion.

☐ Review the main visual/synthetic dashboard for monitors that are red, missing or otherwise abnormal.

☐ Check the portal performance dashboard for CPU, memory and worker-thread anomalies when time permits or when an application issue is reported.

☐ Review the Dynatrace Problems page for persistent problems and follow the 7-day / 30-day trend approach described in the KT.

☐ Investigate ongoing issues immediately when they remain active and materially affect availability/performance.

☐ Verify that recent server/configuration changes are reflected in the shared tracker.

☐ For any new production change, verify the required change tickets/approvals exist before execution.

